.TH PHONE-MCP 1 "2026-07-12" "mcp-server-adb" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
phone-mcp \- Model Context Protocol server for controlling Android phones via ADB
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B phone-mcp
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B phone-mcp
starts a Model Context Protocol (MCP) server that exposes tools for
controlling an Android phone through the Android Debug Bridge (ADB).
It communicates with an MCP-aware AI assistant (such as Claude Desktop
or another MCP client) over standard input/output using the stdio
transport.
.PP
The server exposes tools for phone calls, SMS messaging, contacts,
media playback and recording, app management, UI inspection and
interaction, screen analysis, and map/POI lookups on a device
connected via
.BR adb (1).
.PP
This program takes no command-line arguments. It is intended to be
launched by an MCP client, which is typically configured to run
.B phone-mcp
as a subprocess and communicate with it over stdio.
.SH REQUIREMENTS
A device must be connected and authorized via
.BR adb (1)
before any tool provided by the server can operate on it. Use
.B "adb devices"
to verify connectivity.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B AMAP_MAPS_API_KEY
Optional API key enabling the map/POI lookup tools (AutoNavi/Amap).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR phone-cli (1),
.BR adb (1)
.PP
Full documentation and configuration examples:
.br
https://github.com/hao-cyber/phone-mcp
